«the report page, asserted by substring below»
Demo complete — nothing was spent, and nothing was sent anywhere.

  kno-demo/cases.jsonl               12 eval Cases (8 dev, 4 held back)
  kno-demo/pool.jsonl                3 candidate Assets
  kno-demo/tuning.jsonl              the exported tuning set
  kno-demo/tuning.jsonl.manifest.md  what the export claims, and from what
  kno-demo/kno.db                    every run, score and trace
  kno-demo/.gitignore                written by the demo, so this directory stays out of `git status`

Why the numbers look like this:
  score 1.000 — `fake:` answers every Case with what the Case expects, by
    construction. The run happened, was scored against a declared Goal, cost nothing,
    and sealed a holdout; nobody's agent is perfect.
  deltas +0.0000 — injecting an Asset cannot change a deterministic answer, so no
    Asset measured any effect. The intervals are real; the effects are zero.
  portfolio empty — every corrected interval crosses zero, so nothing earned its
    place. "Include nothing new" is a legal, first-class outcome, and the rejection log
    says why for each Asset.

Now do it with your data:
  1. edit kno-demo/cases.jsonl — one scoreable interaction per line, with a stable id
  2. kno baseline --evals kno-demo/cases.jsonl --agent openai:gpt-4.1 --max-cost-usd 2.00

kno.yaml and KNO_* were not read: the demo is pinned to `fake:` so it cannot bill anyone.
Remove everything with: rm -rf kno-demo
